Package: coxdev
Title: Cox Model Deviance, Gradient, Information and Score Sampling
Version: 0.4.0
Authors@R: c(person("Jonathan", "Taylor", role = c("aut"), email = "jtaylo@stanford.edu"),
             person("Trevor", "Hastie", role = c("aut")),
             person("Balasubramanian", "Narasimhan", role = c("aut", "cre"),
                    email = "naras@stanford.edu"))
Description: Fast computation of the deviance of the Cox proportional
    hazards model, its gradient and the diagonal of its Hessian with respect
    to the linear predictor, the information as a matrix-free linear
    operator, and draws of the score (multinomial, Bernoulli, Fisher
    noncentral hypergeometric or wild), with Efron's or Breslow's ties,
    start times (left truncation), strata and sample weights. The 'C++' code
    is shared with the Python package 'coxdev', and the same seed gives the
    same draws from either.
License: GPL (>= 3)
URL: https://github.com/jonathan-taylor/coxdev
BugReports: https://github.com/jonathan-taylor/coxdev/issues
